        ]>>
        <<ad _ad>>

    <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Nope! Nope! Nope!”</span> He shouts, his voice a mix of panic and disbelief, <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I hate this. Turn it off! Please!”</span>  You chuckle at his dramatic response, though a bit spooked yourself, and remind him that he was the one who had insisted on watching this film in the first place, declaring that it would be ‘fun’. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“I take it back!”</span> He yells, shaking his head vigorously like how Noah does when he doesn’t want to eat something gross on his plate. <span style="Color: LightSteelBlue">“Put on cartoons! Please!”</span> <br>
    <br>
    With a sigh and a grin, you reach for the remote and flip the channel, finding it cute how quickly his bravado vanishes in the face of a scary movie. As the familiar animated show begins to play, you notice his body relax slowly. <span style="Color: LightGreen">Within minutes, he is no longer hiding behind the pillow, though snuggles beside you as you watch the childish show. Laughter eventually begins to bubble from his as he pretends the last 5 minutes of terror never happened. The cozy atmosphere returns and you both lose yourselves in the cheerful antics of the animated characters.</span> <br>
    <<socialChange "Kayden" 3 1>>
